-- Free and solution tracer in the boundary outflow. A steady two phase flow of saturated
-- oil and free gas (Sg = 0.3, immobile connate water) through FREE boundaries, driven by an
-- initial pressure gradient of 10 psi over the 20 ft column. The inflow is the initial fluid
-- state (saturated oil with dissolved gas and free gas), and the gas tracer GT enters with
-- concentration 1 in the free gas through the left boundary (BCTRACER). The solution tracer
-- (gas dissolved in the oil) is initially zero.
--
-- The free gas moves fast, so after 5 days the free tracer is 1 everywhere. At the outflow
-- the gas leaves as free gas (carrying the free tracer, 93 %) and as gas dissolved in the oil
-- (carrying the solution tracer, 7 %), and the solution tracer has not arrived yet. The outflow
-- must therefore not change the concentration of the free tracer in the last cell, which stays 1.
-- If all of the gas outflow is taken as free gas, the last cell drops to 0.93.

RUNSPEC
DIMENS
40 1 1 /

OIL
GAS
WATER
DISGAS

FIELD

UNIFOUT

